From 673f6c936b75beb5b18d339c7878b013c4eb8652 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 23:11:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] CI timings: warn only when the PR's own tests
 explain the wall-time regression
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The CI-timings review item warned on every PR whose CI wall time was >25%
over main's. On 11-01 PRs #546, #548 and #552 were warned for +34..44%
while the tests they added took 9.0 s, 12.7 s and 18.9 s, and #546's shard
deltas went both ways (3/8 +183 s, 2/8 -110 s): CI-wide slowness, not the
diffs. The warnings sat unanswered and the PRs merged with them.

- run_tests_parallel.py gives each per-file pytest --durations=0
  --durations-min=<threshold/4> and prints one '⏱ slow test case <s>s
  <node id>' line per case >= HERMES_TEST_SLOW_CASE_S (default 10, 0 off).
- timings_report.py reads the per-file progress lines and slow-case lines
  from the 'Run tests (...)' job logs it already downloads, and the PR's
  changed test files + added test functions from pulls/<n>/files.
- A regression stays a Warning only when those files took >= 60 s or one
  added case took >= 10 s (files and seconds named); otherwise it is Info:
  'CI wall time +N% vs main; not attributable to this PR (its
  added/changed test files took S s)'. No PR data = the old warning.
- ci-timings job gets pull-requests: read for the files endpoint.

Tests: tests/ci/test_timings_attribution.py,
